@startuml isFcPortExists
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title
isFcPortExists – Check if fc-port exists in a Forwarding-Construct
end title

participant "requestor" as requestor
participant "ForwardingConstruct" as fcRes #LightCyan
participant "JSON Driver" as jd #LightYellow
participant "config.json" as cfg #LightGrey

note over requestor
  - forwardingConstruct
  - ltpUuid
end note

requestor -> fcRes: (forwardingConstruct, ltpUuid)
activate fcRes

fcRes -> jd: read forwarding-construct
activate jd

jd <-> cfg: retrieve control-construct
jd --> fcRes: fc-port list from forwarding-construct
deactivate jd

note over fcRes
  <u>Processing</u>
  - Iterate through fc-port entries in forwardingConstruct
  - Check if any fc-port's logical-termination-point matches ltpUuid
  - Return true if match exists
  - Return false if no match exists
end note

fcRes --> requestor: Boolean (true | false)
deactivate fcRes

@enduml
